-- Index RefreshToken.expiresAt for the cleanup sweep.
--
-- Hand-written rather than generated by `migrate dev`, for the same reason as
-- the previous three migrations: this project connects through Neon's pooled
-- endpoint, where Prisma cannot build the shadow database its drift detection
-- needs, so `migrate dev` misreads the postgis extension as drift and offers to
-- reset. Apply with `prisma migrate deploy`.
--
-- TokenCleanupService selects expired rows here every six hours. RefreshToken
-- is much the largest of the token tables — rotation writes one row per refresh,
-- so roughly 96 per active user per day — and without this the sweep is a full
-- scan of exactly the table it exists to keep small.
--
-- Additive and non-blocking in effect: creating an index takes a lock that
-- blocks writes to this table for the duration. At the current row count that
-- is milliseconds. If this is ever re-run against a table with millions of
-- rows, use CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY instead — which cannot run inside the
-- transaction Prisma wraps migrations in, so it would need to be applied by
-- hand outside the migration.

-- CreateIndex
CREATE INDEX "RefreshToken_expiresAt_idx" ON "RefreshToken"("expiresAt");
